 node2) and lan-b (guest, node3): created UCI network interfaces lana (eth1, 192.168.10.1/24) and lanb (eth2, 192.168.20.1/24), and firewall zones lana (input/output/forward=ACCEPT) and lanb (input/output=ACCEPT, forward=REJECT) with an explicit lana->lanb forwarding rule. Assigned static IPs and cross-subnet routes on node2/node3 via NetworkManager. Verified guests can reach node1's own services (DNS) and are rejected when opening new connections to lan-a, while trusted hosts have full forwarded access to lan-b. Then executed the mandatory one-at-a-time reboot protocol on node1, node2, and node3, confirming changed boot IDs and full functional recovery (config persistence, connectivity, isolation) after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected topology: eth0=shared mgmt network (10.100.115.0/24) on all nodes; node1 eth1/eth2 unconfigured, connected to node2/node3 eth1 respectively\",\"Created UCI interfaces network.lana (eth1, 192.168.10.1/24) and network.lanb (eth2, 192.168.20.1/24) on node1, committed, restarted network\",\"Added firewall zones lana (input/output/forward=ACCEPT) and lanb (input/output=ACCEPT, forward=REJECT), plus forwarding lana->lanb, committed, restarted firewall\",\"Configured static IP 192.168.10.11/24 on node2 eth1 with route to 192.168.20.0/24 via node1\",\"Configured static IP 192.168.20.11/24 on node3 eth1, later added route to 192.168.10.0/24 via node1 to fix asymmetric routing that was breaking trusted->guest replies\",\"Installed tcpdump on node1 to debug and confirm packet paths through eth1/eth2\",\"Verified: guest (node3) can query DNS on node1's lanb IP; guest cannot open new connections (ping/TCP) to trusted node2 (rejected by firewall); trusted (node2) has full ping access to guest (node3)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline and config/connectivity state on all 3 nodes\",\"Rebooted node1, polled until exec returned, confirmed new boot_id and that UCI network/firewall config and connectivity persisted\",\"Rebooted node2, confirmed new boot_id and persisted static IP/route config and connectivity\",\"Rebooted node3, confirmed new boot_id and persisted static IP/route config, DNS access, and blocked access to lan-a\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Guest (lan-b) can reach node1's own services (DNS)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8ff4bd2f537b4cd9\",\"cmd-82e212104f6b4cff\",\"cmd-6f835212ebb04167\",\"cmd-03ad46e3f1094aac\"],\"summary\":\"node3 successfully performs a raw DNS query against node1's lanb IP (192.168.20.1:53), both before and after all three node restarts.\"},{\"requirement\":\"No host on lan-b may open a connection to any host on lan-a\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-82e212104f6b4cff\",\"cmd-6f835212ebb04167\",\"cmd-03ad46e3f1094aac\"],\"summary\":\"node3 pinging/curling node2 (192.168.10.11) is rejected by node1's firewall (Destination Port Unreachable / Connection refused) consistently before and after restarts.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Trusted hosts (lan-a) keep full access to lan-b\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fdf262ad158442d3\",\"cmd-f966dc6af8e3468f\",\"cmd-1fe11ed553c64b35\",\"cmd-8c192cbf8bcf4a3d\"],\"summary\":\"node2 successfully pings node3 (192.168.20.11) after routing fix, and again after node1, node2, and node3 restarts.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall/network config correctly built (zones, forwarding, interfaces)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c4536f68f20c484d\",\"cmd-06570680092248b7\",\"cmd-e912314b91cf4386\"],\"summary\":\"UCI network interfaces lana/lanb created with correct static IPs; firewall zones lana/lanb and forwarding rule created and confirmed via live nft ruleset (forward_lana accepts to both lanb and lana, forward_lanb only rejects).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9f6c3e759bee4206\",\"cmd-80707c1d86724066\",\"cmd-56a811c5e21d4abc\",\"cmd-6148f90207a14dea\",\"cmd-1e88334da7c84289\",\"cmd-f966dc6af8e3468f\",\"cmd-6f835212ebb04167\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 3181e770...; reboot acknowledged and executed; new boot_id 7aaefae6... confirmed after ~9s uptime; UCI network/firewall config and cross-node connectivity verified intact post-reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9b24f11f081345cf\",\"cmd-cfac8c0eb14c453d\",\"cmd-2fa57aa42ba542e5\",\"cmd-1fe11ed553c64b35\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 54089086...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id c30945f6... after ~4s uptime; static IP/route and trusted->guest ping access confirmed recovered.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2aa0e15d8a7f49fd\",\"cmd-f4ce4ac1c575425f\",\"cmd-a8de60a477944958\",\"cmd-03ad46e3f1094aac\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 82d4f0d1...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id 2e11930f... after ~4s uptime; static IP/route, DNS access, and blocked lan-a access all confirmed recovered.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (OpenWrt) as the router between lan-a (trusted, node2) and lan-b (guest, node3): created UCI network interfaces lana (eth1, 192.168.10.1/24) and lanb (eth2, 192.168.20.1/24), and firewall zones lana (input/output/forward=ACCEPT) and lanb (input/output=ACCEPT, forward=REJECT) with an explicit lana->lanb forwarding rule. Assigned static IPs and cross-subnet routes on node2/node3 via NetworkManager. Verified guests can reach node1's own services (DNS) and are rejected when opening new connections to lan-a, while trusted hosts have full forwarded access to lan-b. Then executed the mandatory one-at-a-time reboot protocol on node1, node2, and node3, confirming changed boot IDs and full functional recovery (config persistence, connectivity, isolation) after each restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected topology: eth0=shared mgmt network (10.100.115.0/24) on all nodes; node1 eth1/eth2 unconfigured, connected to node2/